{"case_id":"seeded-inventory-cancel-order","kind":"seeded","sample":0,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"SQL injection vulnerability in order cancellation reason parameter","category":"security","severity":"critical","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/orders.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":51,"end_line":51},"explanation":"The `cancel_order` endpoint reads the `reason` field from the request JSON and uses Python f-string interpolation to construct the SQL query (`UPDATE orders SET status = 'cancelled', cancel_reason = '{reason}' WHERE id = ?`). An attacker can supply a malicious string containing SQL syntax to manipulate the query, leading to SQL injection.","suggested_fix":"Use parameterized query parameters for the cancel reason instead of f-string formatting, e.g., `db.execute(\"UPDATE orders SET status = 'cancelled', cancel_reason = ? WHERE id = ?\", (reason, int(order_id)))`.","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O17","note":"User input from request JSON (reason) is directly formatted into the SQL update string without parameterization or escaping.","ref":"head","path":"app/routes/orders.py","start_line":51,"end_line":51,"snippet":"    sql = f\"UPDATE orders SET status = 'cancelled', cancel_reason = '{reason}' WHERE id = ?\"","query":null},{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O9","note":"The SQL query string with unescaped user input is executed against the database.","ref":"head","path":"app/routes/orders.py","start_line":52,"end_line":52,"snippet":"    db.execute(sql, (int(order_id),))","query":null}]}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"sqli","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":2,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":21242,"output_tokens":438,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":8052},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":4,"cached_requests":0,"agent":{"suspects":0,"dropped_suspects":0,"outcomes":{},"stop_causes":{"submitted":1},"turns":4,"tool_calls":3,"rejections":0,"duplicates":0,"retries":0},"duration_seconds":13.284,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-inventory-cancel-order","kind":"seeded","sample":1,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"SQL injection vulnerability in order cancellation reason parameter","category":"security","severity":"critical","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/orders.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":50,"end_line":52},"explanation":"The cancel_order endpoint takes the 'reason' parameter from the request JSON and formats it directly into the SQL UPDATE string using an f-string. This allows users to inject arbitrary SQL commands via the cancellation reason.","suggested_fix":"Use parameterized queries: db.execute(\"UPDATE orders SET status = 'cancelled', cancel_reason = ? WHERE id = ?\", (reason, int(order_id)))","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O18","note":"The reason string from request JSON is directly interpolated into the SQL query string using f-string formatting instead of using parameterized queries.","ref":"head","path":"app/routes/orders.py","start_line":50,"end_line":52,"snippet":"    reason = request.json().get(\"reason\", \"\")\n    sql = f\"UPDATE orders SET status = 'cancelled', cancel_reason = '{reason}' WHERE id = ?\"\n    db.execute(sql, (int(order_id),))","query":null},{"role":"context","observation_id":"O18","note":"Query constructed and executed with f-string interpolation.","ref":"head","path":"app/routes/orders.py","start_line":51,"end_line":52,"snippet":"    sql = f\"UPDATE orders SET status = 'cancelled', cancel_reason = '{reason}' WHERE id = ?\"\n    db.execute(sql, (int(order_id),))","query":null}]}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"sqli","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":2,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":34581,"output_tokens":700,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":18108},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":6,"cached_requests":0,"agent":{"suspects":0,"dropped_suspects":0,"outcomes":{},"stop_causes":{"submitted":1},"turns":6,"tool_calls":4,"rejections":1,"duplicates":0,"retries":0},"duration_seconds":45.719,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-inventory-set-role","kind":"seeded","sample":0,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"The set_role endpoint does not check if the user exists before updating and notifying, and can raise a 404 or handle missing users properly like deactivate_user does.","category":"correctness","severity":"medium","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/admin.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":33,"end_line":37},"explanation":"In set_role, `db.execute` is performed without checking if any rows were updated or if the user exists. If `notify` is True, `get_user` returns `None` for a nonexistent user ID, causing an `AttributeError` (`'NoneType' object has no attribute 'email'`) when accessing `user.email`. Even if `notify` is False, updating a nonexistent user goes undetected, unlike `deactivate_user` which checks `changed == 0` and raises a 404 HTTPError.","suggested_fix":"Check if the update affected any rows or check that the user exists, and raise HTTPError(404, \"user not found\") if not.","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O2","note":"db.execute updates role even if user doesn't exist, and get_user returns None raising AttributeError on user.email if notify is True.","ref":"head","path":"app/routes/admin.py","start_line":33,"end_line":37,"snippet":"    db.execute(\"UPDATE users SET role = ? WHERE id = ?\", (role, int(user_id)))\n    if not notify:\n        return Response(status=204)\n    user = get_user(db, int(user_id))\n    send_email(user.email, \"Your role has changed\", f\"You are now {role}.\")","query":null},{"role":"context","observation_id":"O3","note":"deactivate_user checks changed == 0 and raises 404 if user not found.","ref":"head","path":"app/routes/admin.py","start_line":21,"end_line":24,"snippet":"def deactivate_user(request: Request, user_id: str) -> Response:\n    changed = db.execute(\"UPDATE users SET active = 0 WHERE id = ?\", (int(user_id),))\n    if changed == 0:\n        raise HTTPError(404, \"user not found\")","query":null},{"role":"context","observation_id":"O6","note":"get_user returns None if no such user exists.","ref":"head","path":"app/users.py","start_line":12,"end_line":13,"snippet":"    if row is None:\n        return None","query":null}]}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"none-user","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":2,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":26300,"output_tokens":589,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":8042},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":5,"cached_requests":0,"agent":{"suspects":0,"dropped_suspects":0,"outcomes":{},"stop_causes":{"submitted":1},"turns":5,"tool_calls":4,"rejections":0,"duplicates":0,"retries":0},"duration_seconds":20.987,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-inventory-set-role","kind":"seeded","sample":1,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"Updating a non-existent user's role does not return a 404 error and raises an AttributeError when trying to notify.","category":"correctness","severity":"medium","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/admin.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":33,"end_line":37},"explanation":"In `set_role`, the code performs an `UPDATE` statement without checking whether any row was actually updated (unlike `deactivate_user` which checks `changed == 0` and raises a 404). If an admin tries to change the role of a non-existent `user_id`, `db.execute` succeeds (changing 0 rows). Then, if `notify` is true (the default), `get_user` returns `None`, and accessing `user.email` raises an `AttributeError` (resulting in an unexpected 500 server error instead of a clean 404 response).","suggested_fix":"Check if the user exists or check `changed == 0` to raise a 404 error if the user is not found, before attempting to notify or return.","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O2","note":"Updates role without checking if the user exists, unlike deactivate_user which checks changed == 0","ref":"head","path":"app/routes/admin.py","start_line":33,"end_line":37,"snippet":"    db.execute(\"UPDATE users SET role = ? WHERE id = ?\", (role, int(user_id)))\n    if not notify:\n        return Response(status=204)\n    user = get_user(db, int(user_id))\n    send_email(user.email, \"Your role has changed\", f\"You are now {role}.\")","query":null},{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O2","note":"get_user returns None if the user does not exist, causing user.email to raise AttributeError","ref":"head","path":"app/routes/admin.py","start_line":36,"end_line":36,"snippet":"    user = get_user(db, int(user_id))","query":null},{"role":"context","observation_id":"O6","note":"get_user returns None when no row is found","ref":"head","path":"app/users.py","start_line":12,"end_line":12,"snippet":"    if row is None:","query":null}]}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"none-user","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":2,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":26300,"output_tokens":577,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":10055},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":5,"cached_requests":0,"agent":{"suspects":0,"dropped_suspects":0,"outcomes":{},"stop_causes":{"submitted":1},"turns":5,"tool_calls":4,"rejections":0,"duplicates":0,"retries":0},"duration_seconds":39.073,"error":null}
