{"case_id":"seeded-werkzeug-number-converter-rename","kind":"seeded","sample":0,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"IntegerConverter and FloatConverter docstrings still refer to the parameter as signed in their prose descriptions.","category":"correctness","severity":"low","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"src/werkzeug/routing/converters.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":183,"end_line":184},"explanation":"In `src/werkzeug/routing/converters.py`, the parameter was renamed from `signed` to `allow_negative`, but the docstring descriptions for `IntegerConverter` and `FloatConverter` still refer to the `signed` parameter.","suggested_fix":"Update the docstrings in IntegerConverter and FloatConverter to refer to `allow_negative` instead of `signed`.","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O31","note":"docstring mentions signed parameter instead of allow_negative","ref":"head","path":"src/werkzeug/routing/converters.py","start_line":183,"end_line":184,"snippet":"    By default it only accepts unsigned, positive values. The ``signed``\n    parameter will enable signed, negative values. ::","query":null},{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O33","note":"FloatConverter docstring mentions signed parameter instead of allow_negative","ref":"head","path":"src/werkzeug/routing/converters.py","start_line":208,"end_line":209,"snippet":"    By default it only accepts unsigned, positive values. The ``signed``\n    parameter will enable signed, negative values. ::","query":null}]}],"matches":[],"expected_total":1,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":52160,"output_tokens":1166,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":28271},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":7,"cached_requests":0,"agent":{"suspects":0,"dropped_suspects":0,"outcomes":{},"stop_causes":{"submitted":1},"turns":7,"tool_calls":5,"rejections":1,"duplicates":0,"retries":0},"duration_seconds":48.87