{"case_id":"seeded-werkzeug-number-converter-rename","kind":"seeded","sample":1,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"Renaming the parameter `signed` to `allow_negative` in `NumberConverter` and its subclasses breaks backwards compatibility for anyone using `signed=...` when defining routing rules, and tests in `tests/test_routing.py` still use `signed=True`.","category":"correctness","severity":"high","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"src/werkzeug/routing/converters.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":142,"end_line":142},"explanation":"The pull request renames the `signed` parameter and attribute to `allow_negative` in `NumberConverter`, `IntegerConverter`, and `FloatConverter`. However, existing tests (`tests/test_routing.py`) still pass `signed=True` to rule definitions, which will result in a `TypeError: IntegerConverter.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'signed'`. Furthermore, renaming public parameters of route converters is a breaking API change for users configuring routing rules.","suggested_fix":"Keep `signed` as an accepted parameter (perhaps with deprecation or aliasing to `allow_negative`), or update all tests and consider deprecation warnings.","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O1","note":"parameter `signed` renamed to `allow_negative`","ref":"head","path":"src/werkzeug/routing/converters.py","start_line":142,"end_line":142,"snippet":"        allow_negative: bool = False,","query":null},{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O1","note":"attribute `self.signed` renamed to `self.allow_negative`","ref":"head","path":"src/werkzeug/routing/converters.py","start_line":150,"end_line":150,"snippet":"        self.allow_negative = allow_negative","query":null},{"role":"context","observation_id":"O27","note":"tests still use `signed=True` which will raise a TypeError with the renamed parameter","ref":"head","path":"tests/test_routing.py","start_line":364,"end_line":364,"snippet":"            r.Rule(\"/bars/<float(signed=True):page>\", endpoint=\"bars\"),","query":null}]}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"rule-strings-break","distance":2,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":1,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":25594,"output_tokens":594,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":12114},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":4,"cached_requests":0,"agent":{"suspects":0,"dropped_suspects":0,"outcomes":{},"stop_causes":{"submitted":1},"turns":4,"tool_calls":3,"rejections":0,"duplicates":0,"retries":0},"duration_seconds":14.579,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-werkzeug-password-compare","kind":"seeded","sample":0,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"Replacing hmac.compare_digest with a standard string equality comparison (==) introduces a timing attack vulnerability when verifying password hashes.","category":"security","severity":"high","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"src/werkzeug/security.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":146,"end_line":146},"explanation":"Comparing password hashes using standard equality (`==`) allows an attacker to measure small differences in response time to determine correct bytes of the hash one by one (timing attack), weakening password hash verification. Constant-time comparison (`hmac.compare_digest`) must be used to prevent this.","suggested_fix":"Restore hmac.compare_digest(_hash_internal(method, salt, password)[0], hashval)","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O1","note":"Standard equality operator (==) short-circuits on the first mismatch, leaking timing information about the hash value.","ref":"head","path":"src/werkzeug/security.py","start_line":146,"end_line":146,"snippet":"    return _hash_internal(method, salt, password)[0] == hashval","query":null},{"role":"context","observation_id":"O2","note":"Previous code correctly used constant-time comparison via hmac.compare_digest.","ref":"base","path":"src/werkzeug/security.py","start_line":146,"end_line":146,"snippet":"    return hmac.compare_digest(_hash_internal(method, salt, password)[0], hashval)","query":null}]}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"timing","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":1,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":14512,"output_tokens":398,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":4024},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":3,"cached_requests":0,"agent":{"suspects":0,"dropped_suspects":0,"outcomes":{},"stop_causes":{"submitted":1},"turns":3,"tool_calls":2,"rejections":0,"duplicates":0,"retries":0},"duration_seconds":11.125,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-werkzeug-password-compare","kind":"seeded","sample":1,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"Replacing hmac.compare_digest with a standard string comparison exposes password hash verification to timing attacks.","category":"security","severity":"critical","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"src/werkzeug/security.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":146,"end_line":146},"explanation":"Using standard equality (`==`) to compare password hashes allows an attacker to measure comparison times and deduce the hash character by character, leading to timing attacks. `hmac.compare_digest` must be used for secure, constant-time comparison of secret hashes.","suggested_fix":"Restore hmac.compare_digest(_hash_internal(method, salt, password)[0], hashval)","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O1","note":"Standard equality operator (==) short-circuits on mismatch, leaking timing information about password hashes.","ref":"head","path":"src/werkzeug/security.py","start_line":146,"end_line":146,"snippet":"    return _hash_internal(method, salt, password)[0] == hashval","query":null},{"role":"context","observation_id":"O2","note":"Previously used hmac.compare_digest for constant-time comparison.","ref":"base","path":"src/werkzeug/security.py","start_line":146,"end_line":146,"snippet":"    return hmac.compare_digest(_hash_internal(method, salt, password)[0], hashval)","query":null}]}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"timing","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":1,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":9360,"output_tokens":361,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":4025},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":2,"cached_requests":0,"agent":{"suspects":0,"dropped_suspects":0,"outcomes":{},"stop_causes":{"submitted":1},"turns":2,"tool_calls":1,"rejections":0,"duplicates":0,"retries":0},"duration_s